# Vulnerability details

## Proof of Concept
When processing transactions, the program assumes that items_len will only be 6 or 9, but does not validate against other possible values. Undefined behavior may result if the incoming data does not conform to the expected format.
If items_len is not equal to 6 or 9, subsequent array access out of bounds or logic errors may occur. For example, if items_len is 7, the line assert items[6].is_list = FALSE; will access an element that is out of the array range, which may cause an exception or data corruption.

```cairo
// Pre eip-155 txs have 6 fields, post eip-155 txs have 9 fields
if (items_len == 6) {
    tempvar is_some = 0;
    tempvar chain_id = 0;
} else {
    assert items_len = 9;
    ...
}
```
### poc
```cairo
use ethers::prelude::*;
use ethers::types::{TransactionRequest, Bytes, U256};
use std::str::FromStr;

async fn send_invalid_items_len_tx() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let client = Provider::<Http>::try_from("rpc")?;

    let fake_data = Bytes::from(hex::decode("f86c808504a817c80082520894095ea7b3decb07fb925c02ed4e870b535f0a271e").unwrap());

    let tx = TransactionRequest {
        to: Some(Address::from_str("0xRecipientAddressHere")?),
        gas_price: Some(U256::from(1000)),
        value: U256::from(1000),
        data: Some(fake_data),  
        ..Default::default()
    };

    let result = client.send_transaction(tx, None).await;

    match result {
        Ok(_) => println!("Transaction accepted, which may indicate a vulnerability with items_len verification."),
        Err(e) => println!("Error detected as expected: {:?}", e),
    }

    Ok(())
}

#[tokio::main]
async fn main() {
    send_invalid_items_len_tx().await.unwrap();
}
```
## Recommended Mitigation Steps
To fix this vulnerability, you can add strict validation of items_len at the beginning of the decode_legacy_tx function:
```cairo
let items_len = [tx_items].data_len;
assert items_len == 6 || items_len == 9;  // Add this line
let items = cast([tx_items].data, RLP.Item*);
```


